mpared to  the quiet focus of experienced acting is  best embodied today in the discourse  about succession actors brian cox and  jeremy strong strong's approach to  acting was profiled in a viral new  yorker piece and though he identifies as  immersive rather than method he seems to  employ a lot of the same techniques for  example he distances himself from his  co-stars to mimic his character's  strained relations and requested to get  actually tear gassed in a scene just for  the authenticity cox a classically  trained scottish actor finds this  approach concerning calling method  acting an american disease he personally  ascribes to a turn it on turn it off  style of acting that frankly sounds a  lot less miserable so is it time to  abandon method acting maybe for the  jared letos of the world on a small  scale leto is no different than anyone  who thinks their job is important enough  to justify making their co-workers lives  miserable his problem is less that he's  taking method too far and more that he's  just being a jerk and all the attention  he gets for doing so undermines the  actors who can use method to carefully  craft psychologically rich performances  overall it seems to us that a technique  invented to facilitate more authentic  performances is now overwhelmingly  drawing attention to the actor as a  performer rather than as a character of  course method acting can still be used  to add quiet truth to a skilled actor's  work our spirits live on in the  whole of time  exist in many vessels  through time that just doesn't make for  the spiciest entertainment weekly  headline but we'd like to give the last  word to sir lawrence olivier who after  learning that his co-star and marathon  man dustin hoffman had gone three days  without sleeping to get into character  allegedly asked my dear boy why don't  you just try acting but what do you guys  think does modern method acting need to  smoke and or touch some grass is jared  leto spoiling method acting 